{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/35018-hedge-town","id":35018,"title":"Hedge Town","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-22T11:12:45-08:00","id":35018,"title":"Hedge Town","content":"I'm aiming to introduce a long established Hedge Town into a chronicle at some point. Luckily for me, it's nothing immediate, as it's a monthly game and early into the chronicle. All the same, best to get started now. Thee basic vibe is a &quot;frontier town/wild west&quot; setting. Lawless bandits vs law dogs, with a lot of honest, hard working hobgoblins stuck in the middle. At its heart, it's a goblin market that grew and grew. I'm not entirely sure how it would navigate the inherent risk of the Gentry (though I feel that paying tribute to them through overly dramatic sacrifices and such would do the job), nor am I completely certain that it's not located in a place the Gentry can access, easily or otherwise. <br /> <br /> Has anyone put together a hedge town? I'm curious what people found that did/didn't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1386-thompry","name":"thompry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1386_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T12:03:26-08:00","id":35048,"title":"","content":"How I have it is a Hedgetown/Goblin Community that isn't founded by, ruled by, or largely made up of changelings will likely be insanity inducing to live in. So they may appear nice or honest and hardworking, but are essentially alien experiences if you try to live in them without trying to change the community.<br /> <br /> But I always like the idea. How close is this Hedgetown to any Freeholds or stable portals to the human world? Is it by any Trods?<br /> <br /> What are the Mayor and Sheriff Like? Are you going to have them mighty/comparable to say a Changeling King?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T11:18:43-08:00","id":37934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thompry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/35018-hedge-town#post35018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone put together a hedge town? I'm curious what people found that did/didn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am working on this subject myself. As my present chronicle is in Central New York, I am drawing from a number of local folklore and history to add a suitable feel to the local Hedge, Freeholds, Trods and a Hob town. Native American legends from the region are FULL of horned river-serpents (dragons), several types of man-eating giants, and several types of not-very-helpful little people. So I am drawing some of the flavor from these legends and the traditions of the early settlers of the state. A HUGE number of Irish immigrants settled here, bringing all sorts of folklore, songs and stories. So there is a great deal to work with. <br /> <br /> <b>Scalperton </b>(Hob Town) <br /> This is a fairly large Hob town in my home campaign. It can be found along a water-trod that occasionally connects with the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erie_Canal\" target=\"_blank\">Erie Canal</a> (if you know the key), but also has some swampy routes through the hedge. Scalperton is a fairly large town of winding streets and a mish-mash of buildings mixing log cabins, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Longhouses_of_the_indigenous_peoples_of_North_America\" target=\"_blank\">native longhouses</a> and colonial stone buildings into a jumbled whole. Permanent shops, rotating day and night markets and the boisterous Silver Goblin Inn are all major features. The denizens of Scaplerton are a mercenary lot, renowned along the trods hereabouts are tough merchants, gamblers and cheats. The town is composed of Drudgemen, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pukwudgie\" target=\"_blank\">Pukwudgies </a>(nasty native Hob), Manogemasak (river elves), Sprights, Enchanted Mortals, some changelings and assorted <i>other beings</i> live here. <br /> <br /> <b>Uses in Campaign</b><br /> The local freehold of Lowbridge has some connections and trade agreements with Scalperton. The <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinus_strobus\" target=\"_blank\">White Pine</a> Covenant keeps the peace, but is not seamless as both sides have conflicting views. Scalperton does sell trade goods with the Fae, some of which includes captured mortals or products derived from them. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}